WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.099 --> 00:00:03.439
If you want to see how Twinkies are hidden
in several shots throughout the movie, then

00:00:03.440 --> 00:00:05.440
stick around to the end of this video.

00:00:05.440 --> 00:00:08.840
[INTRO]

00:00:08.940 --> 00:00:10.940
Ahh 2009.

00:00:10.940 --> 00:00:14.990
It was the end of the decade, Nigahiga was
the biggest YouTuber with less than 2 million

00:00:14.990 --> 00:00:21.380
subscribers, "I'm gonna be telling you guys
all the great wonderful reasons 2009 sucked platypus sh--"

00:00:21.380 --> 00:00:25.780
and a comedy-horror called Zombieland became
the darling of pop-culture in an October noticeably

00:00:25.789 --> 00:00:27.800
void of many horror movies.

00:00:27.800 --> 00:00:28.560
Sounds familiar?

00:00:28.560 --> 00:00:30.360
*Crickets*

00:00:30.369 --> 00:00:33.470
Let's get into the Things You Missed.

00:00:33.470 --> 00:00:36.440
[Things You Missed]

00:00:36.440 --> 00:00:41.170
The film opens up by showing zombies at the US capitol building in Washington DC, something that

00:00:41.170 --> 00:00:44.789
looks like it may be revisited in the sequel,
and after a zoom out you can see some of the

00:00:44.789 --> 00:00:48.429
rides at Pacific Playland, which the characters
would visit at the end of the movie.

00:00:48.429 --> 00:00:51.559
As Columbus is going over the rules, he mentions
an interesting observation.

00:00:52.600 --> 00:00:56.640
"When you’re at your most vulnerable, somehow
they could just smell it."

00:00:56.649 --> 00:01:00.481
This could explain why so many of them gather
at the end of the movie, outside of the fact

00:01:00.481 --> 00:01:04.350
that Wichita and Little Rock already drawing
extra attention to themselves by turning on

00:01:04.350 --> 00:01:05.449
the theme park.

00:01:05.449 --> 00:01:08.969
The opening credits are animated to react
to each of the scenes, and the director's

00:01:08.969 --> 00:01:12.950
credit, Ruben Fleischer, gets jumbled around
so that it reads Ruben Flesh.

00:01:12.950 --> 00:01:16.380
You know, cause zombies eat flesh.

00:01:16.380 --> 00:01:18.920
Tallahassee paints the number 3 on both of
his cars.

00:01:18.920 --> 00:01:22.369
This is probably a tribute to American racecar
driver Dale Earnhardt Jr, who also uses the

00:01:22.369 --> 00:01:25.859
number 3 and can be seen on a poster in Tallahassee's
flashback.

00:01:25.859 --> 00:01:29.250
Columbus never makes it back to Ohio to see
if his parents are still alive, but he does

00:01:29.250 --> 00:01:32.840
mention that they are also paranoid shut ins much
like himself.

00:01:32.840 --> 00:01:35.820
Maybe there's a hint that they are still
alive for the sequel.

00:01:35.820 --> 00:01:39.829
During his flashback, I noticed a very nice
piece of Aqua Teen Hunger Force Art on the

00:01:39.829 --> 00:01:40.829
wall.

00:01:40.829 --> 00:01:43.829
It's probably a sign of things to come because
hunger is the main factor that drives not

00:01:43.829 --> 00:01:46.140
only the zombies but also Tallahassee.

00:01:46.500 --> 00:01:51.000
"WHERE ARE YA YOU SPONGY YELLOW DELICIOUS BASTARDS, WHERE ARE YA?"

00:01:52.680 --> 00:01:55.060
Columbus
also drinks can after can of Mountain Dew:

00:01:55.079 --> 00:01:56.079
Code Red.

00:01:56.079 --> 00:01:59.649
Code Red is usually a term used to describe
a state of emergency, which would be an accurate

00:01:59.649 --> 00:02:02.650
way to label the zombie outbreak seen in the
movie.

00:02:02.650 --> 00:02:05.649
Columbus and his hot neighbor call each other
by their apartment numbers, which keeps up

00:02:05.649 --> 00:02:08.979
the trend of there being no real names used
for most of this movie.

00:02:08.979 --> 00:02:12.670
When she turns into a zombie and comes after
him into the bathroom, the subtle joke is

00:02:12.670 --> 00:02:17.170
that he sprays her with disinfectant spray,
zombies are often also called "the infected",

00:02:17.170 --> 00:02:19.650
so it's kind of funny to think that something
like that would work.

00:02:19.650 --> 00:02:23.650
The Twinkie search takes Columbus and Tallahassee
to Blaine’s Grocery, a name that was later

00:02:23.650 --> 00:02:27.300
used in a 2013 zombie survival game called
State of Decay.

00:02:27.300 --> 00:02:30.690
Wichita and Little Rock's scheme is to make
the boys think that Little Rock is infected

00:02:30.690 --> 00:02:34.480
in order for Wichita to do the honors on her
sister, only to steal the guns and the vehicle.

00:02:34.480 --> 00:02:38.730
That’s a pretty risky plan if you ask me,
how did they know Tallahassee wouldn’t just

00:02:38.730 --> 00:02:41.600
fire without hesitation right about here?

00:02:41.600 --> 00:02:45.480
Tallahassee's longing for a Twinkie continues
after the guys lose all their stuff.

00:02:46.460 --> 00:02:49.720
“Believe it or not, Twinkies have an expiration
date.”

00:02:49.720 --> 00:02:53.580
This is a reference a well-traveled myth that
Twinkies never expire, but in reality they

00:02:53.580 --> 00:02:55.180
last about 25 days.

00:02:55.180 --> 00:02:58.900
If Tallahassee is aware of this fact, that
means almost all of North America was wiped

00:02:58.900 --> 00:03:00.750
out under one month ago.

00:03:00.750 --> 00:03:05.270
“It’s amazing how quickly things can go
from bad to total s***storm.”

00:03:05.270 --> 00:03:08.630
When Columbus and Tallahassee make it to the
next town, a couple of upside-down American

00:03:08.630 --> 00:03:09.630
flags can be seen.

00:03:09.630 --> 00:03:13.940
This could be somewhat of a new flag for Zombieland,
because we also see an inverted star spangled

00:03:13.940 --> 00:03:15.820
banner in the opening shot of the movie.

00:03:15.820 --> 00:03:18.820
There’s also some humorous stuff hidden
in the background of the town scene, like

00:03:18.820 --> 00:03:23.850
a bridal shop plastered with anti-zombie propaganda,
and one store with a no zombies sign, as if

00:03:23.850 --> 00:03:26.290
saying that they weren’t allowed in would
somehow protect them.

00:03:26.290 --> 00:03:28.620
Maybe the owners of that store mixed up zombies
with vampires.

00:03:28.620 --> 00:03:31.800
I’ll come back to analyse the car scene
later in this video, but I’ve just got to

00:03:31.800 --> 00:03:34.780
point out… they waste a LOT of ammo in this
movie.

00:03:48.560 --> 00:03:51.931
In the scene that shows one of Wichita and
Little Rock’s pre-Zombieland scams, this

00:03:51.931 --> 00:03:56.120
gas station employee is the same guy from
the beware of bathrooms example seen two minutes

00:03:56.120 --> 00:03:57.120
into the movie.

00:03:57.120 --> 00:03:58.310
Poor dude just can’t catch a break.

00:03:58.310 --> 00:04:01.520
There’s also a gag that appears a couple
times where the characters reference something

00:04:01.520 --> 00:04:03.080
called “zombie kill of the week.”

00:04:04.180 --> 00:04:06.740
“Very cool.

00:04:06.740 --> 00:04:10.280
But… zombie kill of the week?

00:04:10.290 --> 00:04:11.290
Hmmm no sir.”

00:04:11.290 --> 00:04:13.540
It comes up again later when they get to the
Indian trading post.

00:04:13.540 --> 00:04:15.380
Zombie kill of the week?”

00:04:15.380 --> 00:04:16.880
“Close, but no cigar.

00:04:17.420 --> 00:04:21.400
Zombie kill of the week goes to sister Cynthia
Knickerbocker.”

00:04:23.740 --> 00:04:26.760
I don’t know how Columbus would have known
about this.

00:04:26.770 --> 00:04:29.480
I’m pretty sure there’s no TV or internet
at this point.

00:04:29.480 --> 00:04:32.570
Apparently the idea for ‘Zombie Kill of
the Week’ is actually left over from when

00:04:32.570 --> 00:04:36.180
the script for Zombieland was actually being
considered as a weekly TV show rather than

00:04:36.180 --> 00:04:37.180
a movie.

00:04:37.180 --> 00:04:38.930
But let’s say they do know about Cynthia
Knickerbocker.

00:04:38.930 --> 00:04:42.000
That would help explain this line later on
from Tallahassee.

00:04:42.000 --> 00:04:45.720
“Six people left in the world and one of
them’s Bill ****ing Murray.”

00:04:45.720 --> 00:04:50.460
So, Columbus, Tallahassee, Bill Murray, Wichita,
Little Rock and Cynthia Knickerbocker are

00:04:50.470 --> 00:04:52.790
the six people left, as far as we know.

00:04:52.790 --> 00:04:56.400
Their next stop is at this Native American
gift shop place a location stuffed with even

00:04:56.400 --> 00:04:58.680
more hidden meanings and Things You Missed.

00:05:08.100 --> 00:05:12.080
At the trading post, OK I wouldn’t normally
point out something this random, but this

00:05:12.090 --> 00:05:16.750
hat is the same hat that Jessie wears in Toy
Story 2, I mean it’s the EXACT hat, that’s

00:05:16.750 --> 00:05:18.190
the only reason I bring it up.

00:05:18.190 --> 00:05:22.690
And this scene represents the white man’s
conquest to take control over America and

00:05:22.690 --> 00:05:26.630
the destruction it caused to Native American
communities -- the blatant disregard for Indian

00:05:26.630 --> 00:05:30.240
culture on their journey to commit mass genoci--
-- nah I’m just kidding this is just a fun

00:05:30.240 --> 00:05:31.650
scene where they break stuff.

00:05:31.650 --> 00:05:36.120
Also -- Kemo Sabe, the name of the place they
stopped off in is a phrase used by Tonto in

00:05:36.120 --> 00:05:40.130
the classic Western television series The
Lone Ranger, which oddly enough has come up

00:05:40.130 --> 00:05:42.250
in two consecutive Things You Missed episodes.

00:05:42.250 --> 00:05:44.300
Hi ho Silver, ROLL IT.

00:05:46.340 --> 00:05:47.020
“Why you….

00:05:47.020 --> 00:05:48.360
You Kemosabe.”

00:05:49.280 --> 00:05:51.120
“Kemo… sabe?

00:05:52.040 --> 00:05:54.360
That sounds familiar.”

00:05:54.520 --> 00:05:55.960
“That’s right Kemosabe.

00:05:56.460 --> 00:05:57.680
You trusty scout.”

00:05:57.680 --> 00:05:59.600
“Trusty, scout?”

00:05:59.800 --> 00:06:03.900
So naming this location Kemo Sabe fits in
perfectly with the themes of Zombieland.

00:06:03.900 --> 00:06:07.300
At the beginning they are each rogue scouts,
but in order to thrive, each of them has to

00:06:07.300 --> 00:06:08.590
learn to trust each other.

00:06:08.590 --> 00:06:09.590
Kemo Sabe.

00:06:09.590 --> 00:06:10.590
Trusty scouts.

00:06:10.590 --> 00:06:14.090
Their next destination is Hollywood, where
they stay at Bill Murray’s house, and one

00:06:14.090 --> 00:06:16.540
night they discuss what the best parts of
Zombieland are.

00:06:17.740 --> 00:06:19.180
"No no no. Best thing about Z-land:

00:06:19.300 --> 00:06:20.940
No facebook status updates.

00:06:20.940 --> 00:06:23.180
You know, "Rob Curtis is gearing up for Friday."

00:06:23.180 --> 00:06:24.240
Who cares?”

00:06:24.240 --> 00:06:28.400
The actor that plays Columbus is named Jesse
Eisenberg, and less than one year later he

00:06:28.400 --> 00:06:31.900
would play Facebook founder Mark Zuckerberg
in the David Fincher movie, The Social Network.

00:06:31.900 --> 00:06:37.260
The Social Network was casted in summer of
2009, a bit after Zombieland was shot in February

00:06:37.260 --> 00:06:42.460
2009 -- HOWEVER -- both were produced by Columbia
Pictures and distributed by Sony, so it’s

00:06:42.460 --> 00:06:46.060
possible that when Zombieland was created,
they had they inside scoop that Eisenberg

00:06:46.060 --> 00:06:49.040
was probably going to play Zuckerberg, and
put in that joke.

00:06:49.040 --> 00:06:51.650
Because it isn’t all that funny without
the context.

00:06:52.400 --> 00:06:55.419
But like the discussion about the best parts
of Zombieland, it’s the character relationship

00:06:55.419 --> 00:06:59.419
scenes that make this movie stand out above
many other zombie flicks, like the romantic

00:06:59.419 --> 00:07:01.520
scene between Columbus and Wichita.

00:07:01.520 --> 00:07:04.110
They discuss what each of them was doing in
1997.

00:07:04.110 --> 00:07:06.060
What was I doing in 1997?

00:07:06.060 --> 00:07:11.510
I guess I would have been in pre-K. Wichita
says she saw her first R-Rated movie in ‘97.

00:07:11.510 --> 00:07:14.919
Ironically, my first R-rated movie came out
in 1997 as well.

00:07:14.919 --> 00:07:19.870
I didn’t see it in 1997... obviously...
but we do kind of have that in common.

00:07:19.870 --> 00:07:25.150
When Wichita tells about her first kiss, Columbus
asks her, “you guys use tongue?”

00:07:25.150 --> 00:07:28.680
This may be because he’s still a little
bit traumatized about what happened last time

00:07:28.680 --> 00:07:29.980
he had a crush on a girl.

00:07:39.820 --> 00:07:40.820
Yeah.

00:07:40.820 --> 00:07:44.520
So the girls leave Bill Murray’s house the
next morning, and by the way I find it a little

00:07:44.520 --> 00:07:47.190
hard to believe that Bill doesn't have any
Cubs memorabilia.

00:07:47.190 --> 00:07:50.389
I mean, they had just come off of two division titles
at the time.

00:07:50.389 --> 00:07:53.380
Anyway, the girls go to the theme park and
turn on the power, and I love how the rides

00:07:53.380 --> 00:07:56.760
are just immediately going, like as soon as
the power goes on all the rides just start

00:07:56.760 --> 00:08:00.490
running like something out of a theme park
creepypasta.

00:08:00.490 --> 00:08:04.280
At the end of the movie Tallahassee does finally
get his Twinkie, however, there are four

00:08:04.280 --> 00:08:07.290
Twinkies that he overlooked over the course
of the adventure.

00:08:07.290 --> 00:08:12.240
The first was when they come across the crashed
Hostess truck, but it’s filled with Snowballs.

00:08:13.740 --> 00:08:17.080
"Snowballs? Snowballs?

00:08:17.080 --> 00:08:21.180
Where's the dang Twinkies?!"

00:08:21.300 --> 00:08:25.020
But, if Tallahassee had looked just a little
bit further, he would have found a bunch of

00:08:25.030 --> 00:08:27.270
Twinkies stashed behind the other door of
the truck.

00:08:27.270 --> 00:08:30.600
Then, in the grocery store, he walks right
past the Twinkies while he’s taking out

00:08:30.600 --> 00:08:31.660
this zombie.

00:08:32.600 --> 00:08:34.040
"You got a purdy mouth."

00:08:35.440 --> 00:08:39.300
Just kidding. If any of you have seen this image it's actually Photoshopped. It's not real.

00:08:39.620 --> 00:08:43.110
And finally, in the snack shack, moments after
Columbus blows a bullet shell through the

00:08:43.110 --> 00:08:47.089
last remaining box of Twinkies, Tallahassee
turns on the lights to the storage pantry,

00:08:47.089 --> 00:08:50.280
not sure how he knew where the lightswitch
was, but he somehow overlooks the Twinkies

00:08:50.280 --> 00:08:51.360
sitting on the shelf.

00:08:51.360 --> 00:08:55.820
But there’s one more long yellow treat filled
with a sweet filling; and it comes just after

00:08:55.829 --> 00:08:58.720
Tallahassee loses his car to Wichita and Little
Rock.

00:08:58.720 --> 00:08:59.759
The Hummer.

00:08:59.760 --> 00:09:01.880
“Thank God for rednecks!”

00:09:01.880 --> 00:09:05.700
The Hummer truly is Tallahassee's Twinkie
that he never knew he wanted.

00:09:05.709 --> 00:09:09.889
The yellow metal covering the outside offers
him the protection he needed to survive in

00:09:09.889 --> 00:09:13.810
Zombieland, and the sweet filling is the guns
they find in the back seat, which give them

00:09:13.810 --> 00:09:16.380
a much needed means of fighting back against
the zombies.

00:09:16.460 --> 00:09:20.680
The happiest we see Tallahassee, other than
when he meets Bill Murray, is when he gets

00:09:20.680 --> 00:09:21.960
his two Twinkies.

00:09:23.260 --> 00:09:27.500
“Something about a Twinkie reminded him
of a time not so long ago, when things were

00:09:27.500 --> 00:09:30.930
simple and not so ****ing psychotic.

00:09:30.930 --> 00:09:35.180
It was like if he got a taste of that comforting
childhood treat, the world would become innocent

00:09:35.180 --> 00:09:37.029
again and everything would return to normal.”

00:09:37.029 --> 00:09:41.170
And so it does, when these four survivors
put away their trust issues to become sort

00:09:41.170 --> 00:09:42.230
of like a family.

00:09:42.230 --> 00:09:43.619
But do they stay that way?

00:09:43.619 --> 00:09:46.990
We’ll find out in Zombieland 2, and you’ll
find out some of the Things You Missed in

00:09:46.990 --> 00:09:51.649
next week’s episode, so make sure you subscribe
to CZsWorld for new horrors every week, ring

00:09:51.649 --> 00:09:55.800
that deathbell for notifications and I’ll
see you in the next one.

00:09:55.800 --> 00:09:58.739
Assuming we both survive.

